# LED Fading with ESP32

A simple ESP32 project that demonstrates Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) by smoothly fading an LED in and out. This project introduces the basics of analog output control and PWM programming using the Arduino IDE.

## Project Overview

This project gradually changes the brightness of an LED by increasing and decreasing its PWM duty cycle. Instead of simply turning the LED on or off, the ESP32 creates a smooth "breathing" or fading effect.

## Features

- Smooth LED fade in and fade out
- Uses ESP32 PWM 
- Easy to customize fade speed
- Beginner-friendly code
- Great introduction to PWM

## Components Used

- ESP32 Development Board
- LED
- 220Ω Resistor
- Breadboard
- Jumper Wires

## Wiring

- GPIO 23 → LED Anode (+)
- LED Cathode (-) → 220Ω Resistor → GND

> **Note:** Replace GPIO 23 if your project uses a different output pin.

